<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gyges of Lydia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 680–644 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gyges was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lydia">Lydia</a> from around 680 BCE and founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mermnad-dynasty">Mermnad dynasty</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> tells how he killed the last Heraclid king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/candaules">Candaules</a>, and took his throne and queen. He attacked the Greek cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionia">Ionia</a>, sent rich gifts to Delphi and sought Assyrian help against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cimmerians">Cimmerians</a>, who killed him around 644 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gyges-of-lydia.jpg" alt="Gyges of Lydia" width="320" height="326" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Der_Ring_des_Gyges_(Ferrara_16_Jh).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
